! The index COMPARES set XF -- a fixed bug with no regression test.
!
! HOW THIS WAS FOUND.  mutation_score.py mutated setIndexCmpIndicatorsF
! to leave XF alone, and the mutation SURVIVED the entire suite.  That
! is not a hypothetical defect: StretchExecute's own comment on that
! function records it as a bug that WAS there --
!
!   "This helper used to set only XL/XE/XH, so all five compares left
!    XF stale."
!
! -- fixed earlier in the project, and nothing was ever written that
! would notice it coming back.  A documented past fix with no test is
! an invitation to reintroduce it silently.
!
! THE RULE, Reference Manual p.24 for KV and KC and p.25 for KVI, KVNI
! and KCI, in the same words: "The index-flag and index-comparison
! indicators are set in each of the last two operations; the index
! result indicators are not set in these operations."
!
! WHY XF CAN BE FORCED HERE.  XF is indicator bit 38, and p.41 lets
! BRANCH ON BIT "test and change the contents of positions 20-63 of the
! indicator register" -- so unlike AD (bit 16), XF can be driven to a
! known state before each compare.  That is what makes both directions
! testable in one program: set XF wrong, run the compare, and require
! the compare to have corrected it.
!
! BOTH DIRECTIONS, because a compare that merely ORed the flag in would
! pass the first half.
!
! WEAKER STANDARD, STATED: hand-written from p.24, not transcribed.

        SLC, (8)2700.0
!
! ---- a compare must turn XF ON when the index flag is 1 ------------
START   LX, $X1, WFLAG               ! flag 1, so XF is on after the load
        BBZ, $XF, $+1.0              ! force XF OFF, whatever it was
        BB, $XF, $                   ! hang up if XF on -- the clear failed
        KV, $X1, WFLAG               ! COMPARE VALUE: must set XF from the
                                     !   index word's flag, which is 1
        BZXF, $                      ! hang up if XF off -- the compare did
                                     !   not set it
!
! ---- and OFF when the index flag is 0 ------------------------------
        LX, $X1, WNOFLG              ! flag 0
        BB1, $XF, $+1.0              ! force XF ON, whatever it was
        BZB, $XF, $                  ! hang up if XF off -- the set failed
        KV, $X1, WNOFLG              ! the compare must now CLEAR XF
        BXF, $                       ! hang up if XF on -- the compare only
                                     !   sets, never clears
        B, PASS
!
WFLAG   XW, 1, 1, 0, 1               ! value 1, count 1, flag 1
WNOFLG  XW, 1, 0, 0, 0               ! value 1, count 0, flag 0
PASS    BEW, $
        END, START
